Project policy and approval for AI agents

Usage: shield [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init        Create this project's Shield policy and optionally set up agents, after confirmation
  status      Show policy, integrations and pending requests
  doctor      Check configuration and installation prerequisites; changes nothing
  mcp         Set up agent hooks and MCP, or serve Shield's MCP tools
  protection  Change whether agents may read or change protected settings and policy files
  policy      Show policy or review pending changes and history settings
  pack        Install, update, configure, remove, find or inspect permission packs
  registry    List, add, remove or choose registry sources
  rule        List, add, edit or remove project custom rules
  request     List, inspect, approve or deny stored agent requests
  history     List or inspect agent request decisions and outcomes
  cache       Prepare disposable compiled data from the currently committed policy
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --project <PROJECT>              Select a project; otherwise discover the nearest enrolled ancestor
      --json                           Print one JSON result; commands that change policy refuse JSON mode
      --debug-log-dir <DEBUG_LOG_DIR>  Write private per-process diagnostics in this directory (also `SHIELD_DEBUG_LOG_DIR`)
      --no-debug-log                   Disable diagnostic logging, including automatic debug-build logs
      --cache-dir <CACHE_DIR>          Compiled cache location for init, MCP setup or cache preparation
  -h, --help                           Print help
  -V, --version                        Print version

Start a project:  shield init
Configure agents: shield mcp setup
Inspect policy:   shield status  /  shield policy show  /  shield rule list
Find packs:       shield pack search <query>  /  shield pack info <reference>
Review requests:  shield request list  /  shield request approve <request>
Structured data:  add --json to inspection commands
Terminal color:   NO_COLOR disables color
